<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml' lang='en' style='
	--paragraph-font: "Avenir", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
	--p-font-size: 1.5rem;
	--body-width: 60rem;
	--b-side-margin: 1.5rem;
'>

<head>
<meta charset='utf-8'/>
<title>HTML Patterns</title>
<meta name='author' content='https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0977-2029'/>
<meta name='color-scheme' content='dark light'/>
<meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width'/>
<style>

/* hyperlink */
p a {
	text-decoration: none;
}
p a:hover {
	text-decoration: underline;
}

/* aside-note numbered indicator */
p [id^="aNote_"]::after {
	content: "[" counter(note-indicator) "]";
	counter-increment: note-indicator;
	font-size: smaller;
	line-height: 0;
	vertical-align: super;
}

p span.backup {
	display: none;
}

/* aside-note numbered target */
aside :has(> a[href^="#aNote_"])::before {
	content: counter(note-target) ". ";
	counter-increment: note-target;
}

</style>
</head>

<body style='
	font: var(--p-font-size) var(--paragraph-font);
	margin: 0 var(--b-side-margin);
	max-width: var(--body-width);

	counter-reset: note-indicator note-target;
'>

<p>
<!-- 'p q' for dialogue -->
When Rachel put supper on, her and the girl went and fixed some beds. But wouldn’t any of them come in. <q>She’s been dead long enough to get over that sort of foolishness</q>, I says. Because I got just as much respect for the dead as ere a man, but you’ve got to respect the dead themselves, and a woman that’s been dead in a box four days, the best way to respect her is to get her into the ground as quick as you can. But they wouldn’t do it.
</p>

<p>
<!-- 'p cite' for the name of a work -->
<!--  -->
<cite>As I Lay Dying</cite> is a 1930 Southern Gothic novel by American author William Faulkner.<span id='aNote_uid.1'></span> Faulkner's fifth novel, it is consistently ranked among the best novels of the 20th century.<a id='aNote_uid.2' href='#aTarget_uid.2'><span class='backup'>*</span></a> The title is derived from William Marris's 1925 translation of Homer's <cite><a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odyssey'>Odyssey</a></cite>, referring to the similar themes of both works.
</p>

<aside>

<p><a href='#aNote_uid.1'>^</a> Text.</p>
<p id='aTarget_uid.2'><span class='backup'>* </span><a href='#aNote_uid.2'>^</a> Text.</p>


</aside>

<dl>
	<dt><code>&lt;span id='aNote_uid.1'>&lt;/span></code></dt>
	<dd><code>&lt;p>&lt;a href='#aNote_uid.1'>^&lt;/a> Text.&lt;/p></code></dd>
	<dt><code>&lt;a id='aNote_uid.2' href='#aTarget_uid.2'>&lt;span class='backup'>*&lt;/span>&lt;/a></code></dt>
	<dd><code>&lt;p id='aTarget_uid.2'>&lt;span class='backup'>* &lt;/span>&lt;a href='#aNote_uid.2'>^&lt;/a> Text.&lt;/p></code></dd>
</dl>

</body>

</html>
